 -- Fedora Edition <fedora@example.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:03:43 +0800

cubic-fedora (2026.12.26-fedora1) noble; urgency=low

  * Fixed chroot kernel generation still producing a non-live initramfs.
    Fedora kernel releases such as "7.3.4-300.fc45.x86_64" were truncated
    to "7.3.4-300", so dracut reported "Cannot find module directory" and
    wrote an initramfs without dmsquash-live. The full release is now
    preserved and matched against /lib/modules before dracut runs.
  * dracut failures inside the chroot are now propagated instead of being
    reported as success, and initramfs contents are validated directly
    without depending on lsinitrd being installed on the host.

 -- Fedora Edition <fedora@example.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:34:40 +0800

cubic-fedora (2026.12.25-fedora1) noble; urgency=low

  * Fixed Fedora ISOs still stopping in dracut with "Don't know how to
    handle 'root=live:CDLABEL=...'": Isolinux boot configurations use
    relative initrd names (initrd=initrd.img), which were not matched,
    and /isolinux/initrd.img was missing from the fallback list. Relative
    paths are now resolved against the configuration file's directory.
  * Added an initramfs content check after the boot files are written.
    It inspects gzip/xz/bzip2/zstd/lz4 cpio archives directly (without
    requiring lsinitrd on the host) and aborts generation when any
    written initrd lacks the dmsquash-live module.

