 -- Fedora Edition <fedora@example.com>  Mon, 24 Nov 2026 14:10:00 +0000

cubic-fedora (2026.12.14-fedora1) noble; urgency=low

  * Fixed the dracut emergency shell on the second generated disk
    image ("Warning: /dev/disk/by-label/Fedora-Cimm-Live-45 does not
    exist"):
    - The label references in the boot configurations are now rewritten
      by replacing ANY volume label token (CDLABEL=..., LABEL=...,
      search --label ..., search --fs-label ...) with the final custom
      volume id, regardless of the value it currently references. The
      previous logic only replaced the original volume id, which did
      not match when the boot configurations referenced a different
      (truncated, abbreviated, or historical) label.
    - The replacement value is truncated to 32 characters, to match
      what xorriso writes into the ISO9660 primary volume descriptor.
  * Added a "Reuse the existing compressed Linux file system" check
    button on the Compression page. When checked, the Generate page
    skips recompressing the customized Linux file system (and skips
    copying the boot files), verifies that the squashfs image from the
    previous Generate run exists, and directly regenerates the ISO
    (label references, file system sizes, checksums, and the disk
    image). This makes it fast to test boot changes without waiting
    for the compression step. The normal (full) Generate flow is
    unaffected; when the check button is cleared, the customized Linux
    file system is recompressed as before. If no squashfs image exists
    (the first Generate), an error message asks the user to run the
    normal Generate first. The compression selection is disabled while
    the check button is checked.

