 -- Fedora Edition <fedora@example.com>  Mon, 24 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0000

cubic-fedora (2026.12.12-fedora1) noble; urgency=low

  * Fixed the VirtualBox boot failure of the generated disk image
    ("file '/initrd' not found"):
    - For Fedora family disks whose boot directory was not identified
      (newer releases with unified kernel images, or unrecognized boot
      layouts), the Boot tab still rewrote the boot configuration
      files, replacing the initrd references with a path derived from
      the (empty) boot directory. Since the kernel copy step is
      skipped for such disks, the referenced file did not exist, and
      the generated disk image did not boot.
    - The boot configurations are now left untouched when the boot
      directory was not identified; the original boot files and the
      original boot configurations are retained, so the customized
      disk boots exactly like the original disk.
    - Added the Zstandard compression format to the initramfs
      compression extensions (Fedora initramfs files are Zstandard
      compressed since Fedora 35). Previously, the new initrd file
      name was computed without an extension ("initrd"), which
      matched the reported error path.

