cubic-fedora (2026.12.5-fedora1) noble; urgency=low

  * Hardened all long running processes against "getcwd(): No such
    file or directory" failures (rsync code 3):
    - The rsync copy, extract-root, merge-directory, compress-root,
      and kernel copy steps now explicitly set the working directory
      of the spawned process to the root directory (which always
      exists), instead of inheriting the working directory of the
      application.
  * Note: verify the running version with "cubic-fedora -V" before
    troubleshooting; the startup console output should also include
    "The working directory was changed to ...".

 -- Fedora Edition <fedora@example.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000

cubic-fedora (2026.12.4-fedora1) noble; urgency=low

  * Fixed the rsync failure ("getcwd(): No such file or directory",
    rsync code 3) at the start of the copy step:
    - The application inherits the working directory of the terminal
      it was launched from. If that directory is inside the custom
      root file system image (or any other directory that is deleted
      or unmounted during the run, such as when the Extract step
      unmounts a previous Fedora family root image), then subprocesses
      that call getcwd() (such as rsync) fail.
    - The application now changes its working directory to the user's
      home directory at startup, so subprocesses are immune to the
      launch directory being deleted or unmounted.

